  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `fn[fingerprint]` inside `GraphWithChangingEdges/Fingerprinting` in `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs` is a valid coverage exception. It is on an explicit function with a body, and its fenced commentary gives a substantive reason.\n\nThe reason agrees with the current source:\n- `fingerprint` is only called from `InspectionContext::prepare_read` in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/graph.rs`, after `node_content`, and from `record_is_current`'s `Dependency::Node` branch, also after `node_content`. Both paths read node contents.\n- The test records only an outgoing-edge selection. It computes its expected dependency with `edge_fingerprint`, which hashes node paths and never calls `fingerprint`.\n- `load_evidence` returns `None`, so `record_is_current` is not reached.\n- The trait requires the method, and the test deliberately panics there to guard against content reads, so executing it would break the selection-only assertion.\n\nThe commentary is not redundant. The item carries no `{impl}` or `{test}` reference for the same name, and it cites only the built-in.",
